1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,251
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,376 --> 00:00:05,129
{\an8}Jane has worked out
that Red John is one of seven men.

3
00:00:05,546 --> 00:00:08,758
{\an8}"But Red John also knows
the seven names on Jane's list."

4
00:00:09,258 --> 00:00:11,135
{\an8}I'm gonna give you the seven names

5
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:14,514
{\an8}and I need you to put a GPS bug
on each of their cell phones.

6
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:16,516
- The wires are up.
- All of them?

7
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:18,351
Yep. GPS And audio.

8
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:20,436
Okay. We watch them like hawks.

9
00:00:20,561 --> 00:00:23,898
- We log everywhere they go 24/7.
- Will do.

10
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,776
"We have an anonymous tip
directed to your unit."

11
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:30,696
"A person or persons in distress
at 5570 West Huron."

12
00:00:30,821 --> 00:00:32,323
Brett Partridge is there.

13
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:42,875
Oh, my God.

14
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:47,922
- Partridge?
- Tiger... T... Tiger.

15
00:00:56,055 --> 00:00:57,431
Lisbon, finally.

16
00:00:57,557 --> 00:00:58,724
"I'm sorry, Patrick."

17
00:00:58,849 --> 00:01:01,018
"Teresa can't come
to the phone right now."

18
00:01:21,497 --> 00:01:22,540
Sir?

19
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:26,002
Sir? Are you sure
I can't call you a cab, or...

20
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:28,546
No. You're gracious and kind.

21
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:31,048
"Domo arigato."

22
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:32,550
You're welcome.

23
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,012
Good night.

24
00:02:16,677 --> 00:02:18,095
Oh, no.

25
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:20,765
"Pull the car over to the right."

26
00:02:28,105 --> 00:02:29,857
Oh, no, no, no!

27
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:40,076
Sir, are you aware you crossed
a double yellow line back there?

28
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:42,703
Please, officer,
this is unnecessary.

29
00:02:42,828 --> 00:02:45,122
- You should go.
- Have you been drinking?

30
00:02:45,247 --> 00:02:46,749
No! Not at all.

31
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:50,294
Sir, I'm gonna need you
to step out of the vehicle.

32
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,880
Officer, I'm really sorry
about this.

33
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:55,299
Sir!
Hey, hey, don't...

34
00:02:56,258 --> 00:02:57,593
Son of a...

35
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:23,035
What? It exploded?

36
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,330
Well, how long will it take
to get that under control?

37
00:03:27,164 --> 00:03:30,501
All right, well, when the smoke clears,
let me know and I'll get a team out.

38
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,503
Sheridan, what happened here?

39
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:36,340
We got a call about an hour ago
from your, uh, Agent Lisbon.

40
00:03:36,465 --> 00:03:38,467
Called for immediate assistance
from this address.

41
00:03:38,718 --> 00:03:42,471
Uniforms responded, found
one male D.O.A. and Lisbon down.

42
00:03:42,596 --> 00:03:45,099
- How is she?
- Don't know. The EMTs are with her.

43
00:03:45,224 --> 00:03:47,351
- She ID the body?
- Yeah, we got a...

44
00:03:47,768 --> 00:03:50,062
Brett Partridge.
Worked forensics.

45
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,690
- You know him?
- Uh, slightly.

46
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:56,026
- Jane, how is she?
- I don't know. You got any water on you?

47
00:03:56,235 --> 00:03:58,028
- What?
- I need some water!

48
00:03:58,487 --> 00:04:00,197
Anybody, you got any water?

49
00:04:00,322 --> 00:04:02,158
- Bottle of water! Anybody!
- Over here!

50
00:04:04,368 --> 00:04:05,536
Thank you.

51
00:04:09,248 --> 00:04:10,458
Wait, wait, wait.

52
00:04:37,231 --> 00:04:39,734
- Oh, hey, boss. Feeling better?
- Much. Thanks.

53
00:04:41,569 --> 00:04:42,820
Good morning.

54
00:04:58,252 --> 00:05:00,505
- Sir?
- Oh. Lisbon.

55
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,423
I'll be with you in a minute.

56
00:05:25,655 --> 00:05:26,906
Lisbon...

57
00:05:29,075 --> 00:05:30,493
Give me a hand, would you?

58
00:05:31,035 --> 00:05:32,078
Teresa?

59
00:05:33,788 --> 00:05:35,164
Sorry about this.

60
00:05:37,583 --> 00:05:38,960
Everything's okay.

61
00:05:39,669 --> 00:05:41,212
It's all right.
You're safe.

62
00:05:41,838 --> 00:05:42,880
You're safe.

63
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,675
{\an8}What happened?

64
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:48,010
{\an8}You don't remember anything?

65
00:05:49,345 --> 00:05:51,931
{\an8}Aside from Partridge, no.
Why?

66
00:05:52,431 --> 00:05:53,933
Wh-what'd he do?

67
00:05:54,934 --> 00:05:55,977
{\an8}Nothing.

68
00:05:57,687 --> 00:05:59,897
{\an8}Doctor says
you're completely unharmed

69
00:06:00,356 --> 00:06:01,941
{\an8}apart from a taser burn.

70
00:06:04,652 --> 00:06:06,863
{\an8}- What time is it?
- Morning, sometime.

71
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:10,908
Partridge is dead.

72
00:06:13,244 --> 00:06:17,164
Red John killed him
and did nothing to me. Why?

73
00:06:18,708 --> 00:06:20,251
He didn't do nothing.

74
00:06:22,753 --> 00:06:24,630
He took Partridge's blood...

75
00:06:27,174 --> 00:06:29,886
put it on your face,
made his mark.

76
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:32,179
Okay.

77
00:06:35,933 --> 00:06:37,184
Wh-what does that mean?

78
00:06:38,978 --> 00:06:42,648
{\an8}He was just being playful.
Ran out of time.

79
00:06:43,149 --> 00:06:46,611
{\an8}Maybe something spooked him and
he couldn't go through his usual routine.

80
00:06:48,362 --> 00:06:50,698
{\an8}You were right
about the phone traces.

81
00:06:51,115 --> 00:06:53,159
Red John hooked me
like a fish.

82
00:06:53,284 --> 00:06:56,913
{\an8}- Well, at least he threw you back.
- I'll have Van Pelt pull them down.

83
00:06:57,121 --> 00:06:59,832
{\an8}They're completely illegal,
aside from anything else.

84
00:07:00,082 --> 00:07:01,167
{\an8}There is that.

85
00:07:02,418 --> 00:07:04,337
{\an8}Wait. Well...

86
00:07:05,171 --> 00:07:08,424
{\an8}Before Partridge died,
he looked at me

87
00:07:08,549 --> 00:07:11,636
{\an8}and he said, "Tiger, tiger,"
as in the poem...

88
00:07:11,928 --> 00:07:13,930
{\an8}Which is what Red John
said to you, right?

89
00:07:14,388 --> 00:07:17,308
- That's interesting.
- What does it mean?

90
00:07:17,808 --> 00:07:18,935
I don't know.

91
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:21,812
Hello?

92
00:07:21,938 --> 00:07:23,648
Uh, Ms. Lee? Carmen Lee?

93
00:07:23,981 --> 00:07:25,775
Uh, sorry.
Wrong room, I guess.

94
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,109
Sorry.

95
00:07:31,822 --> 00:07:34,158
{\an8}Red John has been ahead of us
this entire time.

96
00:07:34,283 --> 00:07:37,036
I know you say he's not psychic,
but I'm not sure.

97
00:07:38,955 --> 00:07:41,791
{\an8}You said yourself, when Red John
killed Eileen Turner

98
00:07:41,916 --> 00:07:45,044
it was like he reached inside your head
and killed a happy memory.

99
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:48,047
{\an8}How could he do that
if he's not psychic?

100
00:07:48,714 --> 00:07:50,174
{\an8}That's a good question.

101
00:08:04,063 --> 00:08:06,774
{\an8}"Hi. You've reached the voicemail
of Dr. Sophie Miller."

102
00:08:06,899 --> 00:08:08,859
{\an8}"If this is a true
psychiatric emergency"

103
00:08:08,985 --> 00:08:11,612
{\an8}"please call 911 and seek
immediate assistance."

104
00:08:12,029 --> 00:08:14,031
{\an8}"Otherwise, leave a message,
and I'll get back to you"

105
00:08:14,156 --> 00:08:16,033
{\an8}"as quickly as I can.
Thanks."

106
00:08:16,492 --> 00:08:19,078
{\an8}Sophie? Uh, Patrick Jane.

107
00:08:19,578 --> 00:08:22,039
{\an8}It's been a while.
Uh...

108
00:08:22,164 --> 00:08:26,085
{\an8}Good to hear your voice.
I have something I need to ask you about.

109
00:08:26,252 --> 00:08:29,672
{\an8}Uh, could you give me a call back
when you have a moment?

110
00:08:30,548 --> 00:08:33,009
{\an8}Thank you.
Hope you're well.

111
00:08:40,599 --> 00:08:42,601
- How's the boss?
- Awake and cranky.

112
00:08:42,727 --> 00:08:44,729
- Are they releasing her today?
- Yes, I guess.

113
00:08:45,187 --> 00:08:46,897
Uh-oh. Look out.

114
00:08:47,148 --> 00:08:49,066
So who's in charge
until Lisbon gets back?

115
00:08:49,191 --> 00:08:52,028
{\an8}- I am, sir.
- Well, no rest for the wicked, I'm afraid.

116
00:08:52,153 --> 00:08:54,488
{\an8}A car exploded last night
on Churchill Road.

117
00:08:54,947 --> 00:08:57,074
There's one victim.
Sac P.D.'s already on the scene.

118
00:08:57,199 --> 00:08:59,577
- We'll get on it.
- Yeah, I'll, uh, go with him.

119
00:09:00,661 --> 00:09:02,621
{\an8}I'll check with the P.D.
See what they dug up.

120
00:09:02,747 --> 00:09:03,956
You, Jane?

121
00:09:04,206 --> 00:09:05,791
Oh, I'm, uh, busy.

122
00:09:06,959 --> 00:09:08,335
{\an8}No doubt.

123
00:09:08,461 --> 00:09:10,171
{\an8}Well, it's good news
about Lisbon, huh?

124
00:09:10,796 --> 00:09:12,423
Extraordinarily lucky

125
00:09:12,882 --> 00:09:14,717
Red John sparing her.

126
00:09:14,842 --> 00:09:17,344
- What was she doing there, by the way?
- What do you mean?

127
00:09:17,470 --> 00:09:18,804
Well, when the call came in
about the house

128
00:09:18,929 --> 00:09:21,390
{\an8}there was no mention
of Partridge or Red John.

129
00:09:21,974 --> 00:09:24,351
{\an8}So why did Lisbon go there?

130
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:26,687
Don't know.
Following a hunch, I guess.

131
00:09:26,812 --> 00:09:28,022
A hunch?

132
00:09:28,898 --> 00:09:32,068
Jane, I-I understand your appetite
for secrecy.

133
00:09:32,193 --> 00:09:35,362
I'm even willing to tolerate it...
within limits.

134
00:09:35,988 --> 00:09:37,406
But I'm telling you again.

135
00:09:38,199 --> 00:09:41,160
If you have Red John in your sights
I will be there.

136
00:09:41,952 --> 00:09:42,995
Clear?

137
00:09:44,413 --> 00:09:45,498
Completely.

138
00:09:56,926 --> 00:09:59,720
I think it's Bertram.
We know Red John has major juice.

139
00:09:59,845 --> 00:10:01,514
He has to,
given what he's pulled off.

140
00:10:01,639 --> 00:10:03,974
Bertram's got more juice
than anyone on Jane's List.

141
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,477
No, Bret Stiles runs a worldwide cult
with thousands of followers

142
00:10:06,602 --> 00:10:08,145
and billions of dollars
in assets.

143
00:10:08,604 --> 00:10:10,606
Okay, other than Stiles.

144
00:10:10,856 --> 00:10:12,233
But Bertram's on the inside.

145
00:10:12,358 --> 00:10:14,777
He can keep an eye
on the investigation, hide his tracks.

146
00:10:16,403 --> 00:10:18,155
Tell me I'm wrong.
Go ahead. Bring it on.

147
00:10:18,614 --> 00:10:19,782
I don't think you're wrong.

148
00:10:20,407 --> 00:10:22,326
- Yeah?
- It could definitely be Bertram.

149
00:10:23,828 --> 00:10:24,870
There's something creepy
about him.

150
00:10:24,995 --> 00:10:26,622
There is something creepy
about him, isn't there?

151
00:10:27,998 --> 00:10:30,960
So you're, uh, agreeing with me?

152
00:10:31,085 --> 00:10:33,212
- I guess.
- All right.

153
00:10:35,089 --> 00:10:36,132
Wha!

154
00:10:36,257 --> 00:10:40,010
The crowd goes wild
because Cho agrees with me!

155
00:10:40,136 --> 00:10:41,512
Wha!

156
00:10:45,975 --> 00:10:49,478
I pulled the guy over a little
before midnight. Typical D.U.I.

157
00:10:49,728 --> 00:10:51,313
Driver's giving me some lip.

158
00:10:51,438 --> 00:10:53,524
Then he hits the gas,
and kaboom.

159
00:10:53,649 --> 00:10:57,069
- You run the plates?
- Yeah. Guy's name was Titus Stone.

160
00:10:57,319 --> 00:10:58,988
I sent the ID to your office.

161
00:10:59,905 --> 00:11:02,199
Coroner already took his body
but you're not missing anything.

162
00:11:02,324 --> 00:11:04,994
- Guy was pretty crispy.
- Hey, Cho, look at this.

163
00:11:06,704 --> 00:11:08,706
Hole in the roof
says bomb in the car.

164
00:11:09,165 --> 00:11:10,666
The edges of the hole
are bent inward.

165
00:11:10,916 --> 00:11:12,710
So the bomb was on the outside
on top of the car.

166
00:11:12,835 --> 00:11:14,920
Yeah, but how? It doesn't look like
there was a roof rack.

167
00:11:15,045 --> 00:11:17,173
- How's it stay in place?
- Did you see it explode?

168
00:11:17,298 --> 00:11:19,133
No, but my dashboard
camera caught it.

169
00:11:20,342 --> 00:11:21,886
You wanna see this.

170
00:11:24,889 --> 00:11:26,223
Here we go.

171
00:11:27,224 --> 00:11:30,060
See that thing right there?
What the hell is that?

172
00:11:30,186 --> 00:11:32,438
- Run that again.
- Okay.

173
00:11:34,523 --> 00:11:36,567
There's a light heading for the car
from the front.

174
00:11:37,943 --> 00:11:39,153
Is that something flying there?

175
00:11:39,278 --> 00:11:41,447
Looks like it hits the car
right before it explodes.

176
00:11:41,572 --> 00:11:43,782
- Could it be some kinda missile?
- I doubt it.

177
00:11:45,034 --> 00:11:47,661
- You know, that could be a drone.
- A drone?

178
00:11:48,454 --> 00:11:50,831
- Wow, that's crazy.
- Run it again.

179
00:11:51,373 --> 00:11:53,626
- Sure.
- Excuse me.

180
00:11:54,752 --> 00:11:56,754
- Hey, Grace.
- Hey, good-lookin'.

181
00:11:57,588 --> 00:11:59,924
So I didn't wanna wake you
when I left, but, uh...

182
00:12:00,049 --> 00:12:02,009
that was pretty spectacular
last night.

183
00:12:02,134 --> 00:12:03,427
Yeah, it was.

184
00:12:04,011 --> 00:12:05,638
Hey, I'm free tonight.

185
00:12:05,763 --> 00:12:08,599
Sounds good. So I was thinking,
uh, we should definitely discuss

186
00:12:08,724 --> 00:12:12,019
the, uh, new agenda
with a focus on a significantly

187
00:12:12,144 --> 00:12:14,980
new approach to... something.

188
00:12:15,105 --> 00:12:17,650
- Someone just walk by?
- Yeah.

189
00:12:17,775 --> 00:12:22,071
- What were you calling about?
- Uh, Titus Stone. No arrests.

190
00:12:22,196 --> 00:12:25,449
No family in state. A cousin in Minneapolis.
She's been informed.

191
00:12:25,574 --> 00:12:28,327
He worked for a company
called Modern Aerodynamics.

192
00:12:28,577 --> 00:12:32,289
According to their website,
they design unmanned aerial vehicles.

193
00:12:32,414 --> 00:12:34,458
- "You know what those are?"
- Drones?

194
00:12:34,625 --> 00:12:35,793
How'd you know?

195
00:12:44,510 --> 00:12:45,552
Patrick.

196
00:12:46,679 --> 00:12:47,721
Dr. Miller.

197
00:12:48,722 --> 00:12:49,848
Sophie.

198
00:12:55,521 --> 00:12:57,690
- What's up, Cho?
- Are you working this case?

199
00:12:58,524 --> 00:13:01,735
- I'm always working the case.
- Rigsby's going to the victim's house

200
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:03,821
and I've gotta talk
to some people about drones.

201
00:13:04,822 --> 00:13:06,073
Drones.

202
00:13:06,532 --> 00:13:07,741
That's new.

203
00:13:08,701 --> 00:13:10,577
- Count me in.
- All right. Bye.

204
00:13:21,964 --> 00:13:25,217
Hello. I'm Kris Makkena.
I'm one of the company's presidents.

205
00:13:25,509 --> 00:13:27,094
Agent Kimball Cho, CBI.

206
00:13:27,219 --> 00:13:28,887
- This is Patrick Jane.
- Hello.

207
00:13:30,472 --> 00:13:33,350
I'm sorry. I'm just, uh...
It was a very hard morning.

208
00:13:33,475 --> 00:13:37,521
Um... My partner is in the conference
room, if you'll come this way.

209
00:13:38,439 --> 00:13:40,607
- So you make drones here?
- Uh, we design them.

210
00:13:40,733 --> 00:13:43,485
- We don't manufacture.
- What did Titus Stone do for you?

211
00:13:43,610 --> 00:13:45,696
Titus had been with us
since we started the company.

212
00:13:45,821 --> 00:13:48,907
He was our design chief.
He was a genius. He was our genius.

213
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:50,326
He was... he was brilliant.

214
00:13:50,451 --> 00:13:53,579
Mm, genius and brilliant...
usually synonyms for "difficult."

215
00:13:53,704 --> 00:13:55,414
Uh, well, he was a tad eccentric

216
00:13:55,539 --> 00:13:58,292
and socially awkward at times,
didn't always get people

217
00:13:58,417 --> 00:14:00,377
but at the end of the day,
we all adored him.

218
00:14:01,045 --> 00:14:02,338
I doubt that.

219
00:14:04,757 --> 00:14:05,883
Elliott.

220
00:14:07,593 --> 00:14:09,970
Elliott Winston.
I run the company with Kris.

221
00:14:10,095 --> 00:14:11,930
- Agent Cho, is it?
- That's right.

222
00:14:12,222 --> 00:14:15,351
Our attorney says that you think
a U.A.V. killed Titus.

223
00:14:15,476 --> 00:14:17,686
- Is that true?
- U.A.V...

224
00:14:18,479 --> 00:14:20,814
An unmanned vehicle.
It's a drone.

225
00:14:21,482 --> 00:14:22,733
We're looking into that.

226
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:25,027
- Then why are you here?
- What do you mean?

227
00:14:25,152 --> 00:14:28,697
Our product isn't very popular
in certain quarters outside the country.

228
00:14:28,822 --> 00:14:30,532
Or inside the country,
for that matter.

229
00:14:31,241 --> 00:14:33,535
If a U.A.V. was involved
in this, it's clear...

230
00:14:33,786 --> 00:14:36,914
someone decided to use
poor Titus as a prop

231
00:14:37,039 --> 00:14:40,000
in a particularly grotesque
piece of political theater

232
00:14:40,125 --> 00:14:42,252
- which is simply... simply...
- Oh, Elliott...

233
00:14:42,795 --> 00:14:43,837
terrorism.

234
00:14:44,505 --> 00:14:47,424
The FBI should be here,
not a... state agency.

235
00:14:47,549 --> 00:14:48,842
We're in contact with the FBI.

236
00:14:48,967 --> 00:14:51,762
If we find evidence of terrorism
we'll take the appropriate steps.

237
00:14:51,887 --> 00:14:53,514
But right now it's a homicide.

238
00:14:53,806 --> 00:14:57,142
Now... was Stone having problems
with anyone else here?

239
00:14:57,434 --> 00:15:00,729
Uh... nothing serious,
not that we knew about.

240
00:15:00,896 --> 00:15:03,732
- What was he working on?
- He started a new line of product

241
00:15:03,857 --> 00:15:07,111
uh, but he'd just completed work
on a project called the Redbird

242
00:15:07,236 --> 00:15:09,363
which we delivered
to the military a few months back.

243
00:15:09,488 --> 00:15:11,448
The Redbird?
Well, that's a cool name.

244
00:15:11,573 --> 00:15:14,159
Is that the kind of drone
that shoots missiles

245
00:15:14,284 --> 00:15:17,287
and blows up trucks
and houses, stuff?

246
00:15:17,746 --> 00:15:19,832
- Something like that.
- I see.

247
00:15:20,791 --> 00:15:24,878
- Redbird. Is it red?
- No. Black. What is the point here?

248
00:15:25,003 --> 00:15:29,216
There is none, just that mere mention of it
makes both of you tense. Why is that?

249
00:15:29,341 --> 00:15:32,553
Our work for the Pentagon is covered
by strict confidentiality agreements

250
00:15:32,678 --> 00:15:36,557
so technically, admitting the Redbird exists
is a violation of federal law.

251
00:15:36,682 --> 00:15:38,642
We could all go to jail
just for having this conversation.

252
00:15:38,767 --> 00:15:41,103
Well, that could explain it.
Could.

253
00:15:41,228 --> 00:15:43,730
Some nut out there who thinks
we're war criminals

254
00:15:43,856 --> 00:15:46,817
has drawn a target on our back.
That's who you should be looking for.

255
00:15:46,984 --> 00:15:49,445
Maybe.
Now where does Stone work?

256
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:54,408
This is Nicholas Vashum.
He was Titus' research assistant.

257
00:15:54,533 --> 00:15:55,868
Anything else, let me know.

258
00:15:56,869 --> 00:16:00,497
- Dude. Jane. Cho.
- Hey.

259
00:16:01,331 --> 00:16:02,541
What's with all the bugs?

260
00:16:02,666 --> 00:16:06,211
Oh, um, we've been working on U.A.Vs
that mimic insect flight

261
00:16:06,336 --> 00:16:08,964
and Titus said having images
around helped.

262
00:16:09,089 --> 00:16:11,133
Why would you wanna mimic
insect flight?

263
00:16:11,258 --> 00:16:14,178
So you can make the drone really small
like the size of a mosquito.

264
00:16:14,303 --> 00:16:16,513
It could land on your shirt
and you wouldn't even notice.

265
00:16:17,139 --> 00:16:20,434
- Creepy.
- I guess.

266
00:16:20,559 --> 00:16:22,895
We hear Stone can be difficult.
You have issues with him?

267
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:26,023
No. God, no. No, no.
I got him, you know?

268
00:16:26,148 --> 00:16:27,691
Like, what was in Titus' head

269
00:16:27,816 --> 00:16:29,818
was way more real to him
than what was outside of it.

270
00:16:29,943 --> 00:16:31,945
Like... other people.

271
00:16:32,362 --> 00:16:33,864
Like, he started this diet
a few months back

272
00:16:33,989 --> 00:16:37,159
and if I brought in food
like, any food...

273
00:16:37,284 --> 00:16:41,371
he would throw me outta the room
and say I was sabotaging him and... you know.

274
00:16:42,414 --> 00:16:44,583
- You know.
- What did Stone do in his free time?

275
00:16:45,459 --> 00:16:49,004
Uh, he played a lotta videogames
he watched a lotta movies.

276
00:16:49,254 --> 00:16:50,756
Samurai movies, I'm thinking.

277
00:16:50,881 --> 00:16:53,050
Yeah, he was really
into that kung fu stuff.

278
00:16:53,175 --> 00:16:56,386
More Kurosawa than kung fu.
Was he seeing someone?

279
00:16:56,512 --> 00:16:59,765
You mean, like, a woman?
Um... no.

280
00:16:59,890 --> 00:17:01,183
What about hookers?

281
00:17:03,018 --> 00:17:04,686
What...what makes you think
he did that?

282
00:17:05,896 --> 00:17:09,024
Well, lonely overweight guy goes on a diet...
he's trying to impress someone.

283
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:11,235
Yeah, he didn't...
mention that to me.

284
00:17:12,819 --> 00:17:14,488
What do you know
about the Redbird?

285
00:17:14,613 --> 00:17:18,825
And you can speak freely, 'cause Cho
and I have top level security clearance.

286
00:17:18,951 --> 00:17:21,328
Nothing.
I didn't work much on the Redbird.

287
00:17:21,495 --> 00:17:23,914
Your boss says you get threats
from people who don't like drones.

288
00:17:24,039 --> 00:17:26,375
- That true?
- Yeah. That happens. It's scary.

289
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,794
There's some hardcore haters
out there.

290
00:17:28,919 --> 00:17:30,045
I'll bet.

291
00:17:31,713 --> 00:17:33,006
I'll be outside.

292
00:17:36,843 --> 00:17:38,762
If that's Stone's laptop,
I'm gonna need to take it.

293
00:17:39,429 --> 00:17:41,306
Ooh, uh, I'll have to ask.

294
00:17:41,431 --> 00:17:43,475
It probably has some
classified material on there.

295
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,519
You guys really have
top security clearance?

296
00:17:45,644 --> 00:17:46,812
No.

297
00:17:49,356 --> 00:17:52,025
"Hi. You've reached the voicemail
of Dr. Sophie Miller."

298
00:17:52,150 --> 00:17:54,069
"If this is a true
psychiatric emergency"

299
00:17:54,194 --> 00:17:57,114
"please call 911 and seek
immediate assistance."

300
00:17:57,239 --> 00:17:59,283
"Otherwise, leave a message,
and I'll get back to you"

301
00:17:59,408 --> 00:18:00,826
"as quickly as I can."

302
00:18:08,625 --> 00:18:12,212
Grace, I want you to stop what you're doing
and look up an address for me.

303
00:18:19,318 --> 00:18:21,404
We ran Stone's credit cards.
Jane was right.

304
00:18:21,529 --> 00:18:24,448
He was hiring prostitutes through an escort
service called Private Companion.

305
00:18:24,657 --> 00:18:25,741
You get any names?

306
00:18:25,866 --> 00:18:28,869
Yeah, a woman named Carol Mathews
was with Stone the night before he died.

307
00:18:28,994 --> 00:18:31,163
- Rigsby's bringing her in.
- And what about the laptop?

308
00:18:31,288 --> 00:18:32,915
Any problems
with security clearance?

309
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:35,710
No, we told the FBI we only wanted to look
at his calendar and correspondence.

310
00:18:35,835 --> 00:18:37,503
They're cool with it.
Van Pelt's on it.

311
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,797
- When are you getting out?
- Soon, I hope.

312
00:18:40,089 --> 00:18:41,757
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

313
00:18:41,882 --> 00:18:44,468
Man, they're letting anybody
into the hospital these days.

314
00:18:44,927 --> 00:18:46,637
- Ray.
- Hey, Teresa.

315
00:18:47,471 --> 00:18:48,597
Sorry about this.

316
00:18:51,350 --> 00:18:52,601
What are you doing here?

317
00:18:52,727 --> 00:18:55,813
Well, I heard that my favorite CBI agent
was laid up. I thought I'd stop by.

318
00:18:56,856 --> 00:18:59,567
Oh. Thanks.
Nice suit.

319
00:19:00,234 --> 00:19:01,861
Private sector's treating you all right.

320
00:19:02,695 --> 00:19:04,280
Yeah. I do okay.

321
00:19:06,365 --> 00:19:08,617
- So what happened?
- Oh, nothing.

322
00:19:08,743 --> 00:19:10,077
I...
I scraped my knee.

323
00:19:11,162 --> 00:19:12,288
That's not what I hear.

324
00:19:12,621 --> 00:19:14,749
I hear you were this close
to Red John.

325
00:19:16,667 --> 00:19:18,627
That's some scary stuff.
You okay?

326
00:19:18,878 --> 00:19:22,089
Fine. Yeah, it turns out
Red John isn't so tough.

327
00:19:22,214 --> 00:19:24,049
You know, he barely
laid a hand on me.

328
00:19:26,427 --> 00:19:27,553
Good for you.

329
00:19:28,929 --> 00:19:31,891
Well, th-thanks for...
for coming by. But I'm fine.

330
00:19:32,391 --> 00:19:35,770
I'm... totally fine.

331
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,148
Am I making you
nervous somehow?

332
00:19:39,273 --> 00:19:40,691
- No.
- You sure?

333
00:19:40,816 --> 00:19:42,067
'Cause you're acting
like I'm making you nervous.

334
00:19:42,193 --> 00:19:43,486
No!

335
00:19:44,987 --> 00:19:46,405
Wh-why are you here?

336
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:49,366
You and Jane figure you're pretty close
to catching Red John, right?

337
00:19:50,034 --> 00:19:52,620
Have you got a bead on him,
parameters?

338
00:19:52,745 --> 00:19:55,456
Can't say. Sorry.
Why do you care?

339
00:19:55,581 --> 00:19:57,875
I don't care.
I have clients who care.

340
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,336
Visualize clients.
Why do they care?

341
00:20:02,171 --> 00:20:05,090
You know, I figured this was how
the conversation was gonna go, but...

342
00:20:05,382 --> 00:20:07,176
I came anyway.
You know why?

343
00:20:08,344 --> 00:20:10,262
I like you, Teresa.
I really do.

344
00:20:11,722 --> 00:20:13,432
And one of these days,
you and me...

345
00:20:13,849 --> 00:20:14,975
We'll have a time.

346
00:20:16,769 --> 00:20:17,937
Take care of yourself.

347
00:20:24,527 --> 00:20:26,445
I've gotta get outta here.

348
00:20:30,449 --> 00:20:32,827
Miss Mathews, I don't care
about the prostitution charges.

349
00:20:32,952 --> 00:20:35,037
I'm just interested in what happened
with Titus Stone.

350
00:20:35,162 --> 00:20:36,247
I get it.

351
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:38,624
You work as an escort for the...

352
00:20:38,749 --> 00:20:40,751
Private Companion Agency,
is that right?

353
00:20:41,252 --> 00:20:44,088
Strictly speaking,
I'm a, independent contractor.

354
00:20:44,213 --> 00:20:46,090
That means the company offers
the service

355
00:20:46,215 --> 00:20:49,051
but the terms are negotiated
between the client and me.

356
00:20:49,176 --> 00:20:51,762
Also, they don't pay withholding
or F.I.C.A. taxes.

357
00:20:52,221 --> 00:20:54,473
And Stone was paying
for you to sleep with him?

358
00:20:54,598 --> 00:20:57,101
- That is what was occurring.
- How long had you known Stone?

359
00:20:57,226 --> 00:21:00,396
Like, four months?
He'd call every two, three weeks.

360
00:21:00,521 --> 00:21:02,189
And how would you describe him?

361
00:21:02,314 --> 00:21:05,234
Quiet, not very good
at talking, really.

362
00:21:05,359 --> 00:21:06,819
Not until he got into the role.

363
00:21:07,403 --> 00:21:09,655
- The role?
- Yeah, he's into role-playing.

364
00:21:10,155 --> 00:21:12,491
Oh. And what role did you play?

365
00:21:13,367 --> 00:21:18,289
He's a samurai warrior, and I'm a village
girl he just saved from bandits.

366
00:21:18,664 --> 00:21:21,792
He had a robe and sandals
and a real samurai sword.

367
00:21:21,917 --> 00:21:23,127
It's called a katana.

368
00:21:23,419 --> 00:21:25,629
He would talk about the honorable way
of the warrior

369
00:21:25,754 --> 00:21:28,007
and then I would be grateful
for about a half hour.

370
00:21:31,302 --> 00:21:32,720
What was it? Go on.

371
00:21:33,053 --> 00:21:36,849
You know, when he was talking
about honor in that crazy robe

372
00:21:36,974 --> 00:21:39,685
it's the only time he ever really seemed
comfortable with himself.

373
00:21:41,562 --> 00:21:44,440
You saw him the night
before last, right?

374
00:21:45,441 --> 00:21:46,984
Did he talk about any issues
that he had

375
00:21:47,109 --> 00:21:49,111
- problems with other people in his life?
- No.

376
00:21:50,362 --> 00:21:52,406
He did seem kind of sad, though.

377
00:21:52,865 --> 00:21:56,702
He paid for an extra half hour.
Just, you know, cuddling.

378
00:22:00,247 --> 00:22:01,874
- Grace.
- Boss.

379
00:22:01,999 --> 00:22:04,126
- They let you go?
- Y-yeah. What is that?

380
00:22:04,251 --> 00:22:05,878
A computer from Stone's office.

381
00:22:06,003 --> 00:22:08,172
- Anything on it?
- No, nothing.

382
00:22:08,297 --> 00:22:09,924
No files, no applications.

383
00:22:10,049 --> 00:22:11,967
Even the operating system is gone.
It's been wiped.

384
00:22:12,092 --> 00:22:13,969
- Well, how would you do that?
- You run a program.

385
00:22:14,094 --> 00:22:16,931
But you have to run it five or six times
to a get a disk this clean.

386
00:22:17,222 --> 00:22:19,642
Somebody really wanted to get rid
of something on the drive.

387
00:22:19,767 --> 00:22:21,185
There are fragments of data
here and there.

388
00:22:21,310 --> 00:22:24,855
- I'm trying to put 'em together.
- Keep checking, and, um, Grace...

389
00:22:26,523 --> 00:22:28,150
the surveillance
on the Red John suspects...

390
00:22:28,275 --> 00:22:30,194
- I need you to take it down.
- Really?

391
00:22:30,444 --> 00:22:32,863
Right away, as soon as you can.
Don't leave anything behind.

392
00:22:32,988 --> 00:22:35,366
- Sure. Okay.
- Have you seen Jane?

393
00:22:35,616 --> 00:22:37,785
No. He called a little while ago
needed an address.

394
00:22:37,910 --> 00:22:39,078
Whose address?

395
00:22:59,390 --> 00:23:02,184
Lisbon. You're wondering
who Sophie Miller is?

396
00:23:02,309 --> 00:23:05,187
"She was your psychiatrist
after your wife died."

397
00:23:06,146 --> 00:23:07,481
What made you think of her?

398
00:23:07,606 --> 00:23:09,817
Oh, I don't know.
Doctors, hospitals.

399
00:23:10,109 --> 00:23:13,445
You think Red John learned
about Eileen Turner from her.

400
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:15,030
He must have.

401
00:23:15,155 --> 00:23:17,616
I must've told her a lotta things
I don't remember.

402
00:23:18,117 --> 00:23:20,244
I was on some serious medication.

403
00:23:20,369 --> 00:23:22,037
Well, call me after you talk to her.

404
00:23:22,162 --> 00:23:24,331
- Sure.
- Right after.

405
00:23:24,581 --> 00:23:25,708
Bye.

406
00:24:24,308 --> 00:24:26,935
"The patient showed some treatment
response at the session."

407
00:24:27,061 --> 00:24:30,397
"Hilary continues to exhibit signs
of separation anxiety disorder."

408
00:24:30,564 --> 00:24:31,815
"Her symptoms..."

409
00:25:12,439 --> 00:25:13,899
Oh! Oh!

410
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:24,833
Boss?

411
00:25:26,292 --> 00:25:27,544
Are you okay?

412
00:25:28,711 --> 00:25:32,215
Jane found a dead body.
It was somebody he knows.

413
00:25:33,550 --> 00:25:35,009
Red John killed her.

414
00:25:35,844 --> 00:25:39,055
- Why?
- We think he got information from her.

415
00:25:40,098 --> 00:25:41,891
Jane's talking to the local P.D.

416
00:25:46,146 --> 00:25:48,148
Uh, did you get something
off Stone's computer?

417
00:25:48,273 --> 00:25:49,941
This is the other thing.

418
00:25:50,442 --> 00:25:52,360
I was shutting down
the surveillance like you asked

419
00:25:52,485 --> 00:25:54,070
and I noticed something.

420
00:25:54,779 --> 00:25:56,698
I wasn't looking for it.
It was just there.

421
00:25:56,823 --> 00:25:59,117
It's really weird.
It's happening right now.

422
00:26:06,124 --> 00:26:07,834
And when was the last time
you talked to her?

423
00:26:07,959 --> 00:26:11,129
Uh, a-about five years ago.

424
00:26:14,466 --> 00:26:15,675
Excuse me.

425
00:26:17,927 --> 00:26:19,679
Lisbon, I have to call you back.

426
00:26:21,055 --> 00:26:22,265
Jane, I thought you should know.

427
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:25,268
Three of the Red John suspects
are here together right now.

428
00:26:25,810 --> 00:26:27,145
- Who?
- Bertram

429
00:26:27,270 --> 00:26:29,230
Sheriff McAllister,
and Reede Smith.

430
00:26:29,355 --> 00:26:31,399
They're talking outside
Bertram's office.

431
00:26:39,699 --> 00:26:41,868
And we'll need to track the arrests.

432
00:26:42,785 --> 00:26:43,828
Hello.

433
00:26:44,078 --> 00:26:46,456
Uh, Jane, what you doing?
This is a private meeting.

434
00:26:46,581 --> 00:26:48,291
How was I to know?
Door was closed.

435
00:26:48,416 --> 00:26:49,751
- Agent Smith.
- Jane.

436
00:26:50,460 --> 00:26:52,504
- Sheriff McAllister.
- Tom.

437
00:26:52,629 --> 00:26:53,671
Tom.

438
00:26:54,714 --> 00:26:56,591
Okay, I'll call you Tom then.

439
00:26:58,718 --> 00:27:00,094
So what's the deal, Patrick?

440
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:02,263
Well, as soon as you're done,
I need to talk with you.

441
00:27:02,388 --> 00:27:04,557
Well, we may be some time.

442
00:27:04,682 --> 00:27:07,268
We're discussing
a joint anti-narcotics effort

443
00:27:07,393 --> 00:27:09,854
by the CBI,
the FBI, and Napa County.

444
00:27:09,979 --> 00:27:12,649
A lotta meth in my neck of the woods.
I'd like to see it cleaned up.

445
00:27:12,774 --> 00:27:15,902
Good luck with that.
Uh, carry on discussing your effort.

446
00:27:16,027 --> 00:27:17,070
I'll wait.

447
00:27:18,112 --> 00:27:20,823
So what is it that you would
like to talk about, Jane?

448
00:27:21,199 --> 00:27:24,953
You wanted to know whenever we made
progress on the Red John case.

449
00:27:25,495 --> 00:27:26,955
We've made progress.

450
00:27:27,413 --> 00:27:31,125
Red John just killed the doctor who
treated me during my nervous breakdown.

451
00:27:31,251 --> 00:27:33,836
Maybe... you and I should
discuss this alone.

452
00:27:33,962 --> 00:27:36,422
Well, we're all law enforcement
family here, right?

453
00:27:37,549 --> 00:27:39,175
Sophie Miller. Good woman.

454
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:42,512
He chopped her head off, placed it
in her kitchen oven.

455
00:27:42,762 --> 00:27:45,765
- A gag, I suppose.
- Dear God.

456
00:27:46,641 --> 00:27:48,977
So how is that progress?

457
00:27:49,102 --> 00:27:52,105
Red John killed Sophie Miller
because I'm closing in on him.

458
00:27:52,689 --> 00:27:54,941
He's killed two people
within days now.

459
00:27:55,191 --> 00:27:56,734
He's getting desperate
and a little crazy

460
00:27:56,859 --> 00:27:59,445
and he doesn't realize, but he's made
a terrible mistake.

461
00:27:59,904 --> 00:28:02,782
- That's progress, right?
- What mistake did he make?

462
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:07,287
I would tell you, but I've always gotten
the feeling that this room is bugged.

463
00:28:08,496 --> 00:28:09,539
Wired.

464
00:28:09,914 --> 00:28:11,207
Good seeing you all.

465
00:28:19,007 --> 00:28:20,883
Now what the hell was that
all about?

466
00:28:21,009 --> 00:28:23,052
Exactly how much
does Jane know?

467
00:28:24,178 --> 00:28:27,098
- Well, that is the question, isn't it?
- Yes, it is.

468
00:28:27,557 --> 00:28:30,435
- And it's your job to know the answer.
- I'm doing my best.

469
00:28:36,232 --> 00:28:37,317
Thank you.

470
00:28:43,114 --> 00:28:45,283
So did you see anything that says
one of them is Red John?

471
00:28:46,993 --> 00:28:48,119
No.

472
00:28:50,288 --> 00:28:53,625
I'm sorry about Sophie.
I know she helped you.

473
00:29:00,173 --> 00:29:03,176
Do you wanna be alone?
I'm gonna go back to my office.

474
00:29:03,301 --> 00:29:04,677
- You can come...
- No, no, wait, wait.

475
00:29:07,347 --> 00:29:08,723
I'm waiting.

476
00:29:08,848 --> 00:29:12,101
Red John killed Sophie
because she could identify him.

477
00:29:12,226 --> 00:29:15,647
Now he could've stolen my records
without ever seeing her.

478
00:29:16,356 --> 00:29:18,858
He must have wanted
to meet her, to talk to her.

479
00:29:18,983 --> 00:29:20,526
- Why?
- Well, I don't know why.

480
00:29:20,652 --> 00:29:23,112
Maybe curious about someone
that was close to me.

481
00:29:23,738 --> 00:29:24,781
But he did.

482
00:29:25,281 --> 00:29:27,241
He's been planning this
for a while.

483
00:29:27,533 --> 00:29:30,703
Probably went to see her weeks ago
or maybe even months.

484
00:29:31,037 --> 00:29:33,331
Why not kill her then?
And why kill her now?

485
00:29:33,456 --> 00:29:34,791
Her death would've tipped me off.

486
00:29:34,916 --> 00:29:38,044
He waited until he knew
that I would try to track her down.

487
00:29:39,045 --> 00:29:42,507
He had to have used subterfuge
to get in to see her.

488
00:29:43,508 --> 00:29:45,301
- Like pretend to be a patient?
- Probably.

489
00:29:46,761 --> 00:29:48,221
Then she'd have a file on him.

490
00:29:49,055 --> 00:29:51,641
What good would it be?
It's not like he's gonna tell her the truth.

491
00:29:51,766 --> 00:29:54,310
No, but Sophie had
a very good eye for people.

492
00:29:54,519 --> 00:29:57,063
He may not have been able
to hide everything from her.

493
00:29:57,689 --> 00:29:59,357
We need to get that file.

494
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,568
The local police will let you
into Miller's house.

495
00:30:02,694 --> 00:30:05,405
Her appointment calendar
should be in her office.

496
00:30:05,530 --> 00:30:07,407
You're looking
for a first-time male patient

497
00:30:07,532 --> 00:30:09,992
that's been to see her once or twice
in the past six months.

498
00:30:10,118 --> 00:30:12,745
- Got it.
- Do not tell anyone what you're doing.

499
00:30:12,870 --> 00:30:14,914
Turn off your cell phone
and the GPS in your car.

500
00:30:15,039 --> 00:30:18,167
- You don't know who's watching.
- Okay. If you say so.

501
00:30:21,838 --> 00:30:23,923
What's up? Did you find
something on Stone's computer?

502
00:30:24,048 --> 00:30:25,133
I'll have something soon.

503
00:30:25,258 --> 00:30:28,845
Cho wanted me to tell you that he went
to talk to a guy named Aaron Kalinosky.

504
00:30:28,970 --> 00:30:31,431
Worked for Modern Aerodynamics
until a few months ago.

505
00:30:31,556 --> 00:30:32,598
What's the connection there?

506
00:30:32,724 --> 00:30:35,643
Apparently he's got a lawsuit
against Titus Stone.

507
00:30:37,603 --> 00:30:40,398
- Aaron Kalinosky?
- Uh, just a moment, please.

508
00:30:40,982 --> 00:30:42,191
Give it a run.

509
00:30:55,705 --> 00:30:57,415
- Agent Cho, yes?
- Yes.

510
00:30:57,540 --> 00:31:00,460
- That one of your designs?
- Yeah. It's, uh, self-guided.

511
00:31:00,710 --> 00:31:02,253
It's supposed to wend its way
through the forest

512
00:31:02,378 --> 00:31:04,130
and return
without smashing into a tree.

513
00:31:04,255 --> 00:31:05,882
We'll see if it pulls it off.

514
00:31:06,007 --> 00:31:07,550
- This about Titus Stone?
- Yes.

515
00:31:07,675 --> 00:31:09,969
Poor bastard.
The man was brilliant.

516
00:31:10,094 --> 00:31:11,596
Head and shoulders
above the rest.

517
00:31:12,096 --> 00:31:13,598
Did a samurai kill him?

518
00:31:15,266 --> 00:31:16,684
Sorry. Bad taste.

519
00:31:16,809 --> 00:31:19,020
I understand you were suing him
and Modern Aerodynamics.

520
00:31:19,145 --> 00:31:20,229
Oh, that.

521
00:31:20,354 --> 00:31:24,233
I worked with Titus, Kris, and Elliott
on several projects while I was there.

522
00:31:24,567 --> 00:31:27,695
We were arguing over who owns one
of the designs they're still developing

523
00:31:27,820 --> 00:31:29,405
happens all the time.
Nothing personal.

524
00:31:29,530 --> 00:31:31,073
Did Titus Stone feel that way?

525
00:31:31,199 --> 00:31:33,451
- You're gonna have to ask him.
- Were you friends with him?

526
00:31:34,410 --> 00:31:37,038
I don't know that he had friends.
We got along.

527
00:31:37,163 --> 00:31:38,247
Did you talk to him recently?

528
00:31:38,873 --> 00:31:41,042
- Um...
- Why don't you wanna tell me?

529
00:31:41,292 --> 00:31:45,713
'Cause it's confidential,
and national security and blah, blah, blah.

530
00:31:47,507 --> 00:31:48,549
Here.

531
00:31:52,637 --> 00:31:55,181
Try not to get me arrested
for saying this, okay?

532
00:31:55,306 --> 00:31:57,058
Titus called six weeks ago.

533
00:31:57,975 --> 00:32:00,353
There was trouble with that system
they sold to the military.

534
00:32:00,478 --> 00:32:01,521
The Redbird.

535
00:32:02,104 --> 00:32:03,773
There was an accident
in Afghanistan.

536
00:32:03,898 --> 00:32:06,776
One of the Redbirds missed a target
and hit a civilian home

537
00:32:06,901 --> 00:32:09,111
and there were nine or ten deaths,
big investigation.

538
00:32:09,403 --> 00:32:11,781
Titus was worried that there was
a problem with the guidance system.

539
00:32:11,906 --> 00:32:13,449
He wanted me to look
at the specs with him.

540
00:32:13,741 --> 00:32:16,202
Then... he called back
a few days later.

541
00:32:16,452 --> 00:32:18,538
False alarm.
Everything was fine.

542
00:32:18,663 --> 00:32:19,747
Uh... look out.

543
00:32:21,666 --> 00:32:23,334
See? No hands.

544
00:32:25,378 --> 00:32:27,797
No one will say anything official
about the Redbird.

545
00:32:27,922 --> 00:32:30,007
I talked to a guy I served with
who's at the Pentagon now.

546
00:32:30,132 --> 00:32:33,261
He said, off the record there was
an accident and an investigation.

547
00:32:33,761 --> 00:32:35,930
Apparently it cleared
Modern Aerodynamics.

548
00:32:36,055 --> 00:32:37,974
They think the accident
was caused by local weather.

549
00:32:38,099 --> 00:32:40,685
I guess that's why Stone
called Kalinosky off.

550
00:32:41,102 --> 00:32:42,311
What else do we have?

551
00:32:42,436 --> 00:32:45,565
The techs found fragments
of a drone like this in the wreckage.

552
00:32:45,690 --> 00:32:47,400
It's for surveillance.
No weapons.

553
00:32:47,525 --> 00:32:49,443
But you could attach
a small explosive to it.

554
00:32:49,569 --> 00:32:50,820
- Is that easy to do?
- Nah.

555
00:32:50,945 --> 00:32:52,530
Had to be somebody
who knew what they were doing.

556
00:32:52,655 --> 00:32:54,448
- Co-worker?
- With the added weight

557
00:32:54,574 --> 00:32:58,244
the drone has a range of 4 or 5 miles.
I checked with the other employees.

558
00:32:58,369 --> 00:33:00,371
No one was close enough
that night to launch it.

559
00:33:01,080 --> 00:33:03,958
Yeah, maybe Elliott Winston was right.
Some anti-drone guy did it.

560
00:33:04,083 --> 00:33:06,210
Okay, you know what?
Let's start over.

561
00:33:06,335 --> 00:33:07,962
What did Stone do that night?

562
00:33:08,421 --> 00:33:10,089
Well, he left his house
about 6:30.

563
00:33:10,339 --> 00:33:11,591
Went somewhere.
We don't know where.

564
00:33:11,716 --> 00:33:14,886
Showed up at the restaurant 8:15.
Stayed until 11:50.

565
00:33:15,011 --> 00:33:17,305
A 3-hour dinner by himself?
That's a meal.

566
00:33:17,430 --> 00:33:18,890
Did you get anything
from the computer?

567
00:33:19,015 --> 00:33:20,892
Yeah, but it's just a stream
of numbers.

568
00:33:21,017 --> 00:33:23,477
- I can't make sense of it.
- Well, find somebody who can.

569
00:33:23,603 --> 00:33:25,646
Otherwise, we're back
to the drone people.

570
00:33:25,771 --> 00:33:27,231
Did we get the autopsy report?

571
00:33:27,356 --> 00:33:30,735
- You wanna look at the autopsy results?
- Come on. Don't be so surprised.

572
00:33:31,027 --> 00:33:32,987
Does it say what Stone
had for dinner?

573
00:33:33,821 --> 00:33:36,240
Um... "Contents of stomach."

574
00:33:36,365 --> 00:33:38,659
"Fried chicken, cheeseburger
mashed potatoes"

575
00:33:38,784 --> 00:33:42,163
"French fries, macaroni and cheese
apple pie, and ice cream."

576
00:33:42,288 --> 00:33:43,831
- Yuck.
- Excellent.

577
00:33:44,206 --> 00:33:46,125
Let's bring everyone in tomorrow,
wrap this one up.

578
00:33:46,250 --> 00:33:48,044
- What does that mean?
- Finish.

579
00:33:48,169 --> 00:33:52,006
Uh, move on, concern ourselves
with something more important.

580
00:33:52,131 --> 00:33:53,466
- You know who did it?
- Sure.

581
00:33:53,591 --> 00:33:55,134
Take a look for yourselves.
It's right there.

582
00:33:55,259 --> 00:33:56,344
Where?

583
00:34:07,995 --> 00:34:10,289
Thank you for coming.
This shouldn't take long.

584
00:34:10,414 --> 00:34:13,167
What is all this? Is...
is that Aaron Kalinosky?

585
00:34:13,292 --> 00:34:14,334
- Ah, we'll...
- What's he doing here?

586
00:34:14,460 --> 00:34:16,045
Let you know in a minute.
Please, sit down.

587
00:34:16,170 --> 00:34:18,589
I'm sure you're nervous
called to see the Coppers and all

588
00:34:18,714 --> 00:34:22,718
so, uh, let me reassure you
we know neither of you killed Titus Stone.

589
00:34:23,260 --> 00:34:25,679
I think I speak for both of us
when I say that's true.

590
00:34:25,804 --> 00:34:27,306
- Do you know who did it?
- Yes.

591
00:34:27,431 --> 00:34:29,224
- He killed himself.
- He what?

592
00:34:29,349 --> 00:34:32,102
He was a samurai, and he felt
he'd dishonored himself

593
00:34:32,227 --> 00:34:33,687
so he committed seppuku...

594
00:34:33,812 --> 00:34:36,648
ritual suicide
with his own particular sword.

595
00:34:54,958 --> 00:34:57,211
- Well, what's your evidence?
- His dinner.

596
00:34:57,961 --> 00:34:59,963
Cheeseburger, fried chicken

597
00:35:00,631 --> 00:35:03,550
mashed potatoes,
mac and cheese.

598
00:35:04,259 --> 00:35:05,469
Comfort food.

599
00:35:05,969 --> 00:35:08,263
A condemned man's last meal.

600
00:35:08,388 --> 00:35:11,683
Why would he do that?
H-how had he dishonored himself?

601
00:35:11,809 --> 00:35:13,519
Miss Makkena, you wanna tell us?

602
00:35:13,644 --> 00:35:16,438
- Me? Why?
- Because he told you.

603
00:35:17,523 --> 00:35:19,441
- Uh, no.
- Sure, he did.

604
00:35:19,733 --> 00:35:21,819
He came to you to confess

605
00:35:22,528 --> 00:35:23,946
because he was in love with you.

606
00:35:27,407 --> 00:35:28,450
Kris.

607
00:35:29,618 --> 00:35:30,953
I brought you this.

608
00:35:31,620 --> 00:35:33,872
I thought
I-I won't need it anymore.

609
00:35:35,040 --> 00:35:37,376
- Can I come in?
- Uh, yeah...sure.

610
00:35:37,626 --> 00:35:39,962
- Okay, Titus didn't love me.
- Sure, he did.

611
00:35:40,087 --> 00:35:41,880
He had a photograph of you
on his desk.

612
00:35:42,172 --> 00:35:43,382
He kept it there.

613
00:35:43,507 --> 00:35:46,927
He also hired a hooker that looked exactly
like you. It wasn't hard to see.

614
00:35:47,052 --> 00:35:50,013
He came because he knew
there was a problem with Redbird.

615
00:35:51,140 --> 00:35:53,976
It's what led to those deaths
and you three covered it up.

616
00:35:54,643 --> 00:35:56,812
You made investigators think
it was something else

617
00:35:56,937 --> 00:35:58,522
but he couldn't live with that.

618
00:35:58,647 --> 00:36:00,816
- People died because we screwed up.
- Okay.

619
00:36:00,941 --> 00:36:02,484
There were mistakes.
We all know it.

620
00:36:02,609 --> 00:36:04,945
We lied! To everyone!

621
00:36:06,196 --> 00:36:10,909
- It's not... It isn't honorable.
- I don't even know what that means.

622
00:36:11,034 --> 00:36:13,245
Look, it was a moment.
Okay? That's it.

623
00:36:13,370 --> 00:36:17,040
The point is to collect ourselves
act with grace, and move on

624
00:36:17,166 --> 00:36:20,043
because if we don't
Titus, this company...it's gone.

625
00:36:20,169 --> 00:36:22,004
Me, too. I am done.
You will have ruined me.

626
00:36:23,755 --> 00:36:26,008
- Is that what you wanna do, Titus?
- No.

627
00:36:26,133 --> 00:36:27,843
He told you
what he was gonna do

628
00:36:27,968 --> 00:36:30,262
and you didn't even try
and talk him out of it.

629
00:36:30,387 --> 00:36:33,307
The way I feel right now,
I can't live with myself.

630
00:36:34,766 --> 00:36:38,228
I think you should do
whatever brings you peace.

631
00:36:40,189 --> 00:36:41,690
Who knows?
It could be beautiful.

632
00:36:46,403 --> 00:36:48,238
"So you went to the office"

633
00:36:49,239 --> 00:36:51,825
"and you found the suicide note
on his computer"

634
00:36:51,950 --> 00:36:53,994
"that he told you about,
and you got rid of it."

635
00:37:02,377 --> 00:37:04,213
- Kris... Is this true?
- Look, shut up, Elliott.

636
00:37:04,338 --> 00:37:06,965
- Look, even if it were true...
- I had no idea about Titus, none.

637
00:37:07,090 --> 00:37:09,718
- Even if it were, you can't prove it.
- I'm gonna be sick.

638
00:37:09,843 --> 00:37:11,553
Look, just shut up, okay?
I-I-I have...

639
00:37:11,678 --> 00:37:13,889
- I have nothing to answer for.
- You're right.

640
00:37:14,014 --> 00:37:16,475
We can't prove anything.
Not about the suicide.

641
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:18,727
- But we can prove the cover-up.
- What do you mean?

642
00:37:18,852 --> 00:37:22,648
Agent Van Pelt was able to recover
documents from Stone's computer.

643
00:37:22,773 --> 00:37:26,026
They're just numbers to us
but according to Mr. Kalinosky

644
00:37:26,151 --> 00:37:28,987
they prove that there were flaws
in Redbird's design.

645
00:37:29,279 --> 00:37:31,281
He's out there right now
about to give his statement.

646
00:37:31,406 --> 00:37:34,493
- No.
- Obstruction of justice, fraud

647
00:37:34,660 --> 00:37:36,954
- maybe even manslaughter.
- That's impossible!

648
00:37:37,079 --> 00:37:39,665
- I wiped that disk.
- That sounds like a confession.

649
00:37:39,831 --> 00:37:41,500
- It does, doesn't it?
- I'm done.

650
00:37:41,625 --> 00:37:44,086
Wait, wait. Elliott, hang on. Look,
everything's gonna be all right if we just...

651
00:37:44,211 --> 00:37:46,380
- If we just hang together.
- Hang together? Hang...

652
00:37:47,005 --> 00:37:48,340
Are you insane?

653
00:37:48,465 --> 00:37:51,051
- After what you did to Titus?
- Just don't focus on the negative.

654
00:37:51,176 --> 00:37:54,513
Focus on this. I'm calling my lawyer
and cutting a deal.

655
00:37:55,305 --> 00:37:58,267
You're on your own, Kris.
Good luck.

656
00:38:04,690 --> 00:38:07,109
- I wiped the disk.
- You're right. You did.

657
00:38:07,234 --> 00:38:10,612
Mr. Kalinosky said the data
was just random numbers.

658
00:38:10,737 --> 00:38:12,906
- Gibberish.
- Oops.

659
00:38:14,032 --> 00:38:15,534
Jane, Rigsby's on the phone.

660
00:38:16,201 --> 00:38:19,079
Oh. Okay. Excuse me.
I'll take it in your office.

661
00:38:23,208 --> 00:38:27,546
Miss Makkena, I can't arrest you today
but I will... soon.

662
00:38:32,968 --> 00:38:34,845
- How many names?
- Four.

663
00:38:35,262 --> 00:38:38,724
Ernest Matthewson,
Mitchell Livingston Washburn

664
00:38:39,141 --> 00:38:42,227
- Miguel Vavario, and Jay Roth.
- Roth.

665
00:38:42,686 --> 00:38:45,063
It's from the German rot.
Means "red".

666
00:38:45,897 --> 00:38:48,108
- When did she see him?
- Uh...

667
00:38:51,153 --> 00:38:52,988
About five and a half months ago.

668
00:38:53,113 --> 00:38:55,741
- Do you have the file?
- No. There is no file.

669
00:38:56,199 --> 00:38:57,242
What do you mean?

670
00:38:57,367 --> 00:38:59,036
"Well, I searched the whole office.
It's not here."

671
00:38:59,328 --> 00:39:02,164
I got the department secretary to check
the archived files at the university.

672
00:39:02,289 --> 00:39:03,915
There's no file there, either.
It's gone.

673
00:39:04,249 --> 00:39:06,168
- He took it.
- I'm sorry, Jane.

674
00:39:06,293 --> 00:39:08,211
Oh, it's all right, Rigsby.
Thanks for everything.

675
00:39:08,337 --> 00:39:09,713
We'll see you when you get back.

676
00:39:11,631 --> 00:39:13,550
- Damn it!
- Now, now.

677
00:39:13,967 --> 00:39:16,011
I thought we had something.
I really did.

678
00:39:19,014 --> 00:39:21,892
- Why aren't you more upset?
- Well, I kinda half-expected it.

679
00:39:22,893 --> 00:39:25,604
And I know something
that Red John doesn't.

680
00:39:26,646 --> 00:39:30,984
Sophie dictated her notes.
She couldn't type. Never learned.

681
00:39:31,276 --> 00:39:33,195
She was kinda proud
of the fact.

682
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:36,531
She had a service that transcribed
everything for her.

683
00:39:36,656 --> 00:39:39,159
- Did they keep a copy?
- Very possibly.

684
00:39:42,137 --> 00:39:44,890
"Preliminary diagnostic
session with Jay Roth."

685
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:48,752
"Mr. Roth came in complaining of a recent
issue with severe acrophobia."

686
00:39:48,877 --> 00:39:50,462
- Fear of heights.
- I know.

687
00:39:50,587 --> 00:39:52,172
"He's middle-aged, in good health"

688
00:39:52,297 --> 00:39:55,008
"with no stated prior history
of psychiatric issues."

689
00:39:56,093 --> 00:39:58,178
"He has no living family,
but many friends"

690
00:39:58,303 --> 00:40:00,972
"on whom he relies for company
and emotional support."

691
00:40:02,641 --> 00:40:05,894
"He's well-spoken,
good posture, self-possessed."

692
00:40:06,186 --> 00:40:09,689
"In the waiting room, he sat calmly
in one place needing no distraction."

693
00:40:10,774 --> 00:40:13,235
"Though I note,
he is an excellent whistler."

694
00:40:15,112 --> 00:40:17,531
"His self-presentation is pleasant"

695
00:40:17,656 --> 00:40:21,660
"but there are hints in his behavior
of a damaged and narcissistic personality."

696
00:40:23,286 --> 00:40:26,373
"He says he deals with conflict
and adversity easily, though."

697
00:40:26,832 --> 00:40:29,501
"I'm not convinced
he's being truthful about this."

698
00:40:31,545 --> 00:40:35,048
"In fact, much of what he said,
though spoken convincingly"

699
00:40:35,173 --> 00:40:39,094
"did not match what I can only call
my instinctive response to his presence"

700
00:40:39,511 --> 00:40:43,265
"though I cannot point to identifiable
clinical behaviors that indicate this."

701
00:40:45,392 --> 00:40:48,603
"I sense something deceptive
and dark in his emotional makeup."

702
00:40:50,230 --> 00:40:53,233
"However, there is every indication
that his phobia issues are real..."

703
00:40:53,358 --> 00:40:56,319
"whether acrophobia or some
other phobia remains to be seen."

704
00:40:58,029 --> 00:40:59,406
"An interesting case."

705
00:41:01,384 --> 00:41:03,637
"I look forward to further sessions
with him."


